Package: fsdabridge
Type: Package
Title: Bridge to the FSDA MATLAB Toolbox for Robust Statistics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Nour", "Alterri", email = "nourhm.alterri@studenti.unipr.it",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A thin R surface over the shared FSDA Python engine. Calls any
    routine of the FSDA MATLAB toolbox (forward search regression, robust
    estimators, robust clustering, and more) through 'reticulate' and the
    MATLAB Engine API for Python, with routine-agnostic marshalling of
    matrices, structs, tables and cell arrays into R objects. MATLAB, the
    FSDA toolbox and the 'matlabengine' Python package are required at
    runtime only: the package installs, loads and passes its offline checks
    without them.
License: EUPL (>= 1.2)
Encoding: UTF-8
Suggests:
    reticulate,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: MATLAB (>= R2025b), FSDA MATLAB toolbox, Python (>=
    3.9), matlabengine (Python package matching the MATLAB release)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
